        "descriptions": [
            {
                "value": "Please use the latest version 2.0 of the data set available under: https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202508070641-0 Thermogravimetric analyses (TGA) and micro-scale combustion calorimeter (MCC) experiments were carried out for a study on influences on micro-scale experiments in the context of kinetic modelling of the decomposition of cast polymethyl methacrylate (PMMA). Two different sample configurations (preparation methods) were used for the experiments: pieces and powder.",
